WEBVTT

00:00:13.615 --> 00:00:15.242
CASPIAN: What's that?
那是什么？

00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:16.660
I don't know.
不知道

00:00:16.743 --> 00:00:18.495
Looks like some sort of gold statue.
好像是一座黄金雕像

00:00:20.914 --> 00:00:22.291
(cracks, snaps)

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.970
(wood crackling)

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:39.475
(yells)

00:00:49.943 --> 00:00:51.779
He must have fallen in.
他一定是失足落水

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:54.656
Poor man.
可怜的人

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.366
EDMUND: You mean, "poor lord."
应该说“可怜的勋爵”

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.036
-The crest of Lord Restimar.
-And his sword.
雷斯蒂玛勋爵的头盔

00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:00.496
CASPIAN: We need it.
我们需要它

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.499
(eerie voices murmuring)

00:01:03.582 --> 00:01:04.917
Be careful.
小心点

00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:11.673
LUCY: Your sword hasn't turned to gold.
你的宝剑没有变成黄金

00:01:11.757 --> 00:01:13.175
CASPIAN: Both the swords
are magical.
这两把剑具有魔力

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.803
Here.
给我

00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:20.641
He mustn't have known what hit him.
他肯定不知道发生了什么事

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:22.726
EDMUND: Maybe.
可能吧

00:01:23.977 --> 00:01:25.521
Or maybe he was onto something.
不过也可能是有意为之

00:01:27.648 --> 00:01:28.899
What are you talking about?
此话何解？

00:01:48.877 --> 00:01:50.212
What are you staring at?
你在看什么？

00:01:52.256 --> 00:01:54.383
Whoever has access
to this pool...
来到这个水池边的人

00:01:56.176 --> 00:01:58.512
...could be the most powerful
person in the world.
都有可能成为世界上的首富

00:02:02.307 --> 00:02:05.352
Lucy... we'd be so rich.
露西，我们可以发大财

00:02:06.061 --> 00:02:07.980
No one could tell us what to do.
再也不用看人脸色

00:02:08.063 --> 00:02:09.731
Or who to live with.
或是寄人篱下

00:02:09.815 --> 00:02:12.151
You can't take anything
out of Narnia, Edmund.
你不能带走纳尼亚的一草一木，埃德蒙

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.153
Says who?
谁说的？

00:02:15.112 --> 00:02:16.196
I do.
我

00:02:23.912 --> 00:02:25.330
I'm not your subject.
我可不是你的臣民

00:02:26.039 --> 00:02:28.041
You've been waiting for this, haven't you?
你是不是做梦都想夺权

00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:30.169
To challenge me.
You doubt my leadership.
你想挑战我？你怀疑我的领导能力？

00:02:30.252 --> 00:02:31.587
You doubt yourself.
是你怀疑自己

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.922
-You're a child!
-And you're a spineless sap!
-你这毛孩子
-你这没骨气的傻瓜

00:02:34.006 --> 00:02:36.842
-Edmund.
-I'm tired of playing second fiddle.
我已经厌倦了坐第二把交椅

00:02:36.925 --> 00:02:39.344
First it was Peter, and now it's you.
从前是彼得，现在是你

00:02:39.428 --> 00:02:41.930
You know I'm braver
than both of you.
其实我比你们两个勇敢多了

00:02:42.014 --> 00:02:44.057
Why do you get Peter's sword?
为什么是你继承彼得的宝剑？

00:02:44.141 --> 00:02:46.393
I deserve a kingdom of my own.
我应该有自己的王国，应该自己当国王

00:02:46.477 --> 00:02:47.895
I deserve to rule!
我应该有自己的王国，应该自己当国王

00:02:47.978 --> 00:02:50.314
If you think you're so brave, prove it!
你说你勇敢没用，证明给我看

00:02:50.397 --> 00:02:52.149
(yells)
你说你勇敢没用，证明给我看

00:02:53.317 --> 00:02:55.819
No! Stop it!
不

00:02:56.737 --> 00:02:58.280
Both of you!
都给我住手

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:00.657
Look at yourselves.
瞧瞧你们

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.243
Can't you see what's happening?
难道你们还不明白吗？

00:03:04.077 --> 00:03:05.913
This place has tempted you.
这里是诱惑之地

00:03:06.955 --> 00:03:08.290
It's bewitching you.
你们已经受到诱惑

00:03:09.082 --> 00:03:11.335
This is exactly what Coriakin
was talking about.
当初克里亚金曾经语重心长告诫过我们

00:03:12.753 --> 00:03:14.129
Let's just get out of here.
我们马上离开这儿

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.232
(eerie voices murmuring)

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.323
Oh, yes, follow the imaginary Blue Star
是的，跟随想像中的什么蓝星

00:03:41.406 --> 00:03:43.367
to the island of Ramandoodoo.
是的，跟随想像中的什么蓝星

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.035
(steam whooshing)
前往子虚乌有的拉曼杜岛
将七把宝剑放到狮王的餐桌上

00:03:45.119 --> 00:03:47.371
Lay the seven steak knives
at the table of the talking lion.
前往子虚乌有的拉曼杜岛
将七把宝剑放到狮王的餐桌上

00:03:47.454 --> 00:03:50.207
(snorts) Ninnies.
前往子虚乌有的拉曼杜岛
将七把宝剑放到狮王的餐桌上

00:03:52.418 --> 00:03:54.128
(steam whooshes, hisses)

00:04:01.385 --> 00:04:03.804
What is th-- (grunting)
那是什么？

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:17.860
I must be dead.
我一定在做梦

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:43.093
(startled shout)

00:04:45.637 --> 00:04:46.972
You're definitely dead.
你肯定不是做梦

00:04:53.812 --> 00:04:55.314
Won't be needing that then, will you?
你用不着这些了，对吗？

00:05:02.029 --> 00:05:04.823
(eerie growl echoes from distance )

00:05:11.705 --> 00:05:14.917
Finally, a favorable turn of events.
我终于时来运转了

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.086
(eerie voices murmuring)
我终于时来运转了

00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:25.969
What food did you find?
找到什么食物了？

00:05:28.472 --> 00:05:30.390
It's volcanic, Your Majesty.
这是火山岛，陛下

00:05:30.474 --> 00:05:32.059
Not much grows.
寸草不生

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.645
Where's Eustace?
尤斯塔斯去哪儿了？

00:05:36.063 --> 00:05:39.525
I believe he's out,
not helping us load the boats.
肯定是不想帮着装船偷懒去了

00:05:39.608 --> 00:05:40.818
LUCY: Eustace!
尤斯塔斯

00:05:41.902 --> 00:05:43.112
Eustace!
尤斯塔斯

00:05:43.195 --> 00:05:44.905
(steam hisses)
尤斯塔斯

00:05:46.615 --> 00:05:48.242
Edmund, I've got a bad feeling.
埃德蒙，我有种不祥的预感

00:05:49.159 --> 00:05:50.160
I'll go find him.
我去找他

00:05:50.994 --> 00:05:51.995
I'll come with you.
我跟你一道去

00:05:52.079 --> 00:05:54.957
(rumbling continues in distance)
我跟你一道去

00:06:02.548 --> 00:06:03.715
CASPIAN: Eustace!
尤斯塔斯

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.635
EDMUND: Eustace!
尤斯塔斯

00:06:12.307 --> 00:06:13.475
EDMUND: Treasure.
宝藏

00:06:15.853 --> 00:06:17.312
Trouble.
麻烦

